kkim 7 2 9 24 3 27 48 3 51 \nContd………5/- \n\n \n-5- \n24 Tamil Nadu 387 684 1071 377 693 1070 328 398 726 \n25 Telangana       39 115 154 \n26 Tripura 16 01 17 17 Nil 17 10 02 12 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 1123 2726 3849 1083 2068 3151 874 2023 2897 \n28 Uttarakhand 220 154 374 195 127 322 135 95 230 \n29 West Bengal 158 61 219 2668 249 2917 3399 432 3831 \nUnion Territories \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |478", "t": "Science Express Climate Action Special Train", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK  SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.478 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nSCIENCE EXPRESS CLIMATE ACTION SPECIAL TRAIN \n \n478.     SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE: \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has launched a climate change Special \nScience Express Train to put forward the message of climate \nchange; and  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the details of the schedule of \nthis train in Maharashtra State with halting stations marked? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA)  \n \n(a) Yes, Madam. Science Express is a flagship initiative of Department \nof Science & Technology, Government of India.  In the current \nphase, it is run as Climate Action Special jointly by Department of \nScience & Technology and Ministry of Environment, Forest and \nClimate Change. Ministry of Railways pro vides operational support \nin running of the train. \n(b) The train is scheduled from 15 th October, 2015 to 7 th May, 2016.  \nThe train will cover 64 cities in 20 States. The details of the \nschedule of this train including halting stations in Maharashtra are :  \nHalt Station         Date  \nButibori               13-15th April, 2016 \nJalamb                16-18th April, 2016      \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |479", "t": "Skill Loans to Youth", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED   QUESTION   No. 479 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2nd DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nSKILL LOANS TO YOUTH \n \nQUESTION \n \n479 : SHRI SHRI KIRTI AZAD:              \n  \n Will the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP be pleased \nto state: \n \n \n(a) whether the Government provides/proposes to provide skill loans to youth; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the criteria fixed therefore; \n \n(c)            whether the Government proposes to increase the amount of loan; \n \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the role of State Governments in this regard; and \n \n (e)    the time by which the loan amount is likely to be increased? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF SKILL \nDEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY) \n \n \n \n(a) to (e)  Yes. A Skill Loan Scheme was launched by the Hon’ble Prime Minister on \n15.7.2015 with a view to support youth who wish to go through skill training programmes  \nin the Country. This Skill Loan Scheme replaced earlier Indian Banks Association (IBA) \nModel Loan Scheme for Vocational Education and Training. Bank of India has been the \nfirst bank to notify such a skill loan scheme. \n \n Any Indian National who has secured admission in a course run by Industrial Training \nInstitutes (ITIs), Polytechnics or in a school recognised by Central or State education \nBoards or in a college affiliated to recognised university, training partners affiliated to \nNational Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) Sector Skill Councils, State Skill Mission, \nState Skill Corporation, preferably leading to a  certificate/diploma/degree issued by such \norganisation as per National Skill Qualification Framework (NSQF) is eligible for a skilling \nloan. Loans may be given from 5,000/ - to 150,000/- depending on the NSQF level at a \nsimple rate of interest during the study period till commencement of repayment i.e. \nbetween 11% and 12 % by different banks and no processing fee would be charged by \nBanks/Money Financing Institutions. The repayment of loan will have following tenures. \nAt present there is no proposal to increase the amount of loan. \n \n    Sl No Amount of Loan Tenures \n1 Loans upto Rs. 50,000 Upto 3 years \n2 Loans between Rs.50,000 to Rs 1 lakh Upto 5 years \n3 Loans above 1 lakh Upto 7 years. \n \n********* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |48", "t": "Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan in Jharkhand", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †48 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 30TH NOVEMBER, 2015 \n \nSarva Shiksha Abhiyan in Jharkhand \n \n   \n†48. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SINGH:        \n \n  Will the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT मानव संसाधन �वकास \nमंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the total amount of funds spent  under Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) in Jharkhand \nincluding district Chatra during the last three years and current year; and \n \n(b) the total number of primary schools  and the p ost of teachers sanctioned for the \nupgradation under SSA in Jharkhand during the last three years, year-wise? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a): The total amount of funds spent under Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA)  in Jharkhand \nincluding district Chatra during the last three years and current year is as below:- \nSl. No. Financial Year Funds spent (Rs. in Lakhs) \n \n1. 2012-13 168512.02 \n2. 2013-14 76713.20 \n3. 2014-15 125100.30 \n4. 2015-16 (upto 31.10.2015) 69923.39 \n \n(b): The total number of primary schools and the post of teachers sanctioned for the \nupgradation under SSA in Jharkhand during the last three years is as below:-  \nSl. No. Year Primary schools sanctioned \nfor upgradation \n \nPost of teachers sanctioned \n1. 2012-13 0 0 \n2. 2013-14 0 0 \n3. 2014-15 82 246 \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |480", "t": "Railway Stations in Dahod", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.480 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nRAILWAY STATIONS IN DAHOD \n \n† 480. SHRI JASVANTSINH SUMANBHAI BHABHOR: \n              \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the number of railway stations declared as model stations in the \nparliamentary constituency of Dahod during the last three years; \nand \n \n(b)  the requirements identified for the model stations and the tasks \nundertaken to fulfil these requirements? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b): Zone-wise/District-wise details of stations falling under any \nparticular parliamentary constituency is not maintained. Further, the \nModel Station Scheme for upgradation  of amenities at stations was in \nvogue upto year 2008. Since the year 2009, station upgradation is \ndone under the Adarsh Station Scheme. Selection of railway stations \nfor inclusion of stations under the Adarsh Station Scheme is based on \nidentified needs fo r upgradation of amenities at stations and is a \ncontinuous, on-going process. \n*** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |481", "t": "Revenue through Advertisements", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.481 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nREVENUE THROUGH ADVERTISEMENTS  \n \n481.  SHRI SUNIL KUMAR MONDAL: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Railways propose to earn revenue through \nadvertisements over its various properties; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof  and the revenue earned by the Railways \nthrough advertisements during the last three years and the \ncurrent year; and \n \n(c)  the steps taken by the Railways to increase income through \nadvertisements? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( c) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 481 BY SHRI SUNIL KUMAR MONDAL  TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 02.12.2015 REGARDING REVENUE \nTHROUGH ADVERTISEMENTS.  \n \n(a): Yes, Madam. \n \n(b): Comprehensive guidelines exist for generating revenue through \ncommercial advertisements by utilizing various assets of Railways like \nstation premises, trains, approaches to the major stations , Road over \nBridges (ROBs), Road under Bridges (RUBs) etc. Railway-wise details of \nrevenue earned through advertisements during the last three years and \nthe current year are as under: \n(`. in Crores) \nRailway 2012-13 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 \nUpto Aug’ \n2014 \nCentral 34.63 45.04 38.06 15.68 \nEastern 5.20 6.38 6.62 0.61 \nEast Central 2.86 1.82 3.01 0.41 \nEast Coast 4.63 5.76 3.51 1.38 \nNorthern 52.80 13.06 23.84 9.88 \nNorth Central 3.21 3.11 3.62 1.45 \nNorth Eastern 3.20 3.33 3.56 0.82 \nNortheast Frontier 1.28 1.47 1.21 0.46 \nNorth Western 4.09 7.03 6.14 0.79 \nSouthern 32.77 33.69 37.41 18.30 \nSouth Central 10.12 9.72 11.78 4.62 \nSouth Eastern 1.87 3.10 2.83 1.08 \nSouth East Central 1.68 1.95 2.49 1.20 \nSouth Western 11.86 18.92 15.20 5.81 \nWestern 40.86 55.74 58.14 24.92 \nWest Central 3.77 5.14 5.98 3.03 \nMetro 12.08 12.89 19.02 4.00 \nTotal 226.91 228.15 242.42 94.44 \n   \n(c): To assess the earning potential/value of select media assets of \nIndian Railway, Rail India Technical and Economic Services (RITES) has \nbeen directed to facilitate selection  of a Professional Media Market \nEvaluation Agency (PMMEA) , which would identify and assess  the \npotential for additional revenue generation through advertisements. \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |482", "t": "MoU for Atomic Energy", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.482 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nMoU FOR ATOMIC ENERGY \n482.  SHRI  ARKA KESHARI DEO: \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Government has signed any Memorand um of Understanding        \n (MoU) with other countries for the generation and production of atomic energy \n in future which is economical and clean; and \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the steps taken  in this regard, country-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES & PENSIONS AND \nPRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH) :     \n \n(a) Yes Sir. \n \n(b)  India has signed Nuclear agreements/Memorandum  Of Understanding/Joint \nDeclarations with USA, France, Russia, Namibia, Mon golia, Republic of \nKorea, Argentine Republic, United Kingdom, Republic  of Kazakhstan, \nCanada, Sri Lanka and Australia. Out of these the I nter-Governmental \nAgreement (IGA) signed with Russia is for construct ion of nuclear power plant \nat Kudankulam (KKNPP 1 - 4), the Pre-Engineering Ag reement (PEA) signed \nwith M/s AREVA, France is for assessment of license ability of the Evolutional \nPressurised Reactor (EPR) project proposed to be se t up in Jaitapur and \nPreliminary Contract for Technical Feasibility Stud y for AP 1000 reactors \nsigned with Westinghouse Electric Company (WEC), US A is for the proposed \nSite  at Mithivirdi Site in Bhavnagar, Gujarat. \n \n*****  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |483", "t": "e-Transactions", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(DEPARTMENT OF ELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 483 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 02.12.2015 \n \n \nE-TRANSACTIONS \n \n483 PROF.  SAUGATA  ROY: \n                    \n Will the Minister of Communications & Information Technology be pleased to state: - \n \n(a) whether the Government intends to develop a mechanism to do all transactions through e-\nroute;   \n \n(b)      if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)  the proposed time schedule for the project? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY   \n(SHRI RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD) \n \n(a)  to (c): Yes, Sir. Government is implementing National e -Governance Plan (NeGP) since \n2006 which emphasized on increasing delivery of Government to Citizen (G2C) services \nthrough e-route. Under the Digital India programme , NeGP has been transformed into    “e -\nKranti” with emphasis on delivery of all G2C services through e-route. \n \nGovernment has set up a platform called “e -Taal” to measure the e -Transactions on real time \nbasis. \n \n******** \n  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |484", "t": "Non-Governmental Organisations", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 484 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nNon-Governmental Organisations \n \n484.  SHRI S.P. MUDDAHANUME GOWDA: \nWill the Minister of Minority Affairs be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of Non -Governmental Organizations (NGOs) functioning under her \nMinistry in the country for the welfare of minority communities, State-wise; \n(b) the details of schemes that were implemented during the Eleventh Plan Period for the \nwelfare of minorities in the country especially in social, economic and educational \nfields; \n(c) the funds allocated, released and utilized for the said purpose during each year of \nEleventh Plan  and the current year, State and scheme-wise; \n(d) whether the funds allocated under these schemes h ave not been fully utilized by the \nState Governments; and \n(e) if so, the reasons therefor and measures taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a) The State -wise number of Non-Governmental Organisations (NGOs )/ Project \nImplementing Agencies (PIAs) functioningunder various schemes of the Ministry  of \nMinority Affairsand its Autonomous Bodies during 2015-16 are at Annexure I. \n \n(b) During Eleventh Plan Period  (2007-2012), under educational empowerment the \nschemes of Pre -matric Scholarship, Post -matric Scholarship, Merit -cum-Means based \nScholarship, Maulana Azad National Fellowship (MANF) , Free coaching and Allied \nSchemes and Grant -in-Aid to Maulana  Azad Education Foundation (MAEF) ; under \neconomic empowerment, the scheme of equity contribution to National Minorities \nDevelopment and Finance Corporation ( NMDFC) for extending concessional loans;  \nunder area development, the scheme of Multi -sectoral Development Programme; and \nunder social empowerment, the scheme of Computerisation of Waqf Records of State \nWaqf Boards were implemented for the welfare of notified minority communities.   \n \n(c) Allocation of funds under the schemes of the Ministry is not made State -wise. Under \nScholarship andMsDPSchemes,the State -wise and year -wise details of funds  \nreleased and utilized during 11th Plan and current year i.e. 2015-16 are at Annexure II \nto V. Furtherunder Computerisation of Waqf Records of State Waqf Boards,  the  \nfunds are released to State Waqf Boards, Central Waqf Council and National \nInformatics Centre (NIC). Theyear-wise details of funds released during 11 th Plan and \ncurrent year i.e. 2015-16 are at Annexure VI. \n \nUnder MANF, funds are allocated to University Grant Commission (UGC). \nThese are not allocated State -wise. The y ear-wise details of funds released and \nutilized during 11th Plan and current year i.e. 2015-16 are at Annexure VII. \n\n \nIn case of Free Coaching and Allied Scheme, it is implemented by the \nMinistry through selected Non-Governmental Organisation (NGOs). Details of year-\nwise funds released  by Ministry  to NGOs working in various States is given at \nAnnexure VIII.  \n \nCentral Government contributes its share of equity to NMDFC. Under Equity \nContribution to NMDFC,the details of equity contributed during 11th Plan and current \nyear are given at Annexure IX.Under Grant in Aid to MAEF, the Ministry releases \nfunds for the corpus of MAEF. The details of funds released to MAEF are also given \nat Annexure IX. \n \nFurther during current year 2015 -16, the new schemes started during 12th Plan \n(2012-2017) are also under implementation namely, Nai  Roshni, Seekho aur  Kamao, \nJiyo Parsi, Padho Pardesh, Nai Udaan, Strengthening of State Waqf Boards, USTTAD \nand Hamari  Dharohar. All the above schemes are Central Sector Schemes and \nimplemented directly by the Ministry through selected Project Implementing Agencies \nall over the country. The details of fund earmarked, released and utilized under the \nabove schemes during current year 2015-16 are given below: \n(Rs. in crore) \nS.N\no. \nSchemes Earmarked Budget     Funds released and \nutilized (as on \n31.10.2015) \nRemarks \n1. Seekho \naurKamao \n67.45 34.34 The earmarked budget \nhas been enhanced to \nRs.192.45 crore  during \n1st supplementary. \n2. NaiRoshni 15.00 8.72 - \n3. Hamari \nDharohar \n10.01 3.59 - \n4. USTTAD 17.01 0.09 - \n5. JiyoParsi 2.00 1.02 - \n6. PadhoPardesh 4.19 1.63 - \n7. NaiUdaan 4.00 2.01 - \n8. Strengthening of \nState Waqf \nBoards \n6.70 3.04 - \n \n(d) and (e)  During 11 th Plan, u nder the schemes of Scholarship  andMsDP, the funds  \nwere released through the State Governments. In case of Scholarships, funds have \nbeen utilised by the States/ UTs. From current year 2015-16, the Scholarship Schemes \nhave become online under Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) mode on National \nScholarship Portal. The last date of submission of application under Scholarship was \n31.10.2015. So applications duly scrutinized by States/ UTs have not been received \nby the Ministry as on date.   \n \nUnder MsDP, the utilisation of funds by States/ U nion Te"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |485", "t": "Proposal for Tori-Shivpur-Kathotia Line", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 485 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nPROPOSAL FOR TORI-SHIVPUR-KATHOTIA LINE \n \n†485.  SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SINGH: \n  \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether the Railways had proposed laying of Tori -Shivpur-Kathotia \nrailway line;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the estimated cost of the line and \nthe funds released for the same so far;   \n(c)   the current status of the said line; and  \n(d)   the time by which it is likely to be completed? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) to (d):  Yes, Madam. Tori-Shivpur-Kathautia new line project has been \ntaken up at an anticipated cost of `3596 crores and funds to the tune of \n`958 crores have been released by M/s Central Coalfields Limited for this \nproject upto March 2015. The project has been taken up in two phases \nas detailed below: \n(i) Tori-Shivpur (44 km) section at an anticipated cost of `1589 crore. In \nthis section, about 74% land has been acquired and earthwork, \nbridgeworks have been taken up. \n(ii) Shivpur-Kathautia(49 km) section at an anticipated cost of `2007 \ncrores. Alignment has been staked on the ground and land plans \nsubmitted to the State Government for land acquisition. \nThe timeline for completion of the project has not been fixed due to \nuncertainty in acquisition of land and forestry clearances. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |486", "t": "Aid to Countries", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.486 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nAID TO COUNTRIES \n \n486.   SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY: \nDR. VIRENDRA KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether India has given aid to other nations in the last three \nyears for reconstruction, economic development and \nmitigation of environmental disasters; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, year and country-wise; and \n(c) the benefits accrued to these countries through these funds? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n (a) to (c) Information in respect of aid to countries has been \ncompiled and placed at Annexure. \n \n***** \n\n1 \n \nANNEXURE \nAID TO COUNTRIES \n \nFinancial \nYear \n \nCountry \n \nDetails of Aid Provided/benefits accrued to these countries through these funds Amount (Rs.) \n2012-13 Republic of Congo Cash grant – humanitarian assistance-accidental fire(USD 500,000) 2.601 Crores \nNiger Supply of 100 computers and printer towards capacity building 0.621 crores \nLiberia Supply of 25 buses 0.443 crores \nMali Grant for support to the African led International support Mission in Mali (USD 1 \nmillion) 5.408 crores \n Bhutan India provides broad-based multi sectoral development assistance to Bhutan.  \nOur developmental aid has contributed to socio -economic development and  further \nstrengthened our bilateral cooperation with Bhutan in diverse fields, including areas of \nhydropower, infrastructure and connectivity, health, agriculture and irrigation, rural and \ncommunity development, education and training defence and security cooperation. \nNon Plan  Plan \n1171.06 \ncrore \n1538 \ncrore \n Republic of \nDominica \nHumanitarian assistance after flash floods.  \nThe aid given by India has been helpful to the countries in tiding over the effects of \nnatural disasters, helped in capacity building in improvement of their infrastructure. \n \nUS $300,000 \n Saint Lucia Humanitarian assistance after flash floods.  \nThe aid given by India has been helpful to the countries in tiding over the effects of \nnatural disasters, helped in capacity building in improvement of their infrastructure. \nUS $500,000 \n Saint Vincent and \nthe Grenadines \nHumanitarian assistance for  floods.  \nThe aid given by India has been helpful to the countries in tiding over the effects of \nnatural disasters, helped in capacity building in improvement of their infrastructure. \n \nUS $500,000 \n Total aid for \nCapacity Building \nwhich includes aid \nDPA-II Division provided aid/loan/ advances and disaster relief in countries of the \nSouth.  ITEC also forms an important component in the aid which aims at skill \ndevelopment, transfer of technology and sharing experiences with the partner countries \nRs.21049.34 lakhs \n\n2 \n \nfor Disaster Relief \nof Rs.2729.63 lakh \nto Republic of \nCongo, Bangladesh, \nLibya, Fiji, \nPhilippines, \nMyanmar, Syria, \nComoros, \nSeychelles, \nGuatemala, yemen  \n Nepal  India provides broad-based multi sectoral development assistance to Nepal.  \n \nOur developmental aid has contributed to socio -economic development and further \nstrengthened our bilateral cooperation with Nepal in diverse fields, inc luding areas of \ninfrastructure and connectivity, health, agriculture and irrigation, rural and community \ndevelopment, education and training, defence and security cooperation, water resources \nincluding river embankments and hydropower. \n \n305.06 crores \n Sri Lanka GOI is committed to assisting the Government of Sri Lanka in resettlement and \nrehabilitation of Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) in Northern and Eastern Sri Lanka.  \nIn this regard, the Government has been implementing several developmental projec ts, \nparticularly in the areas of development of rail and port infrastructure, connectivity and \ntransportation, agriculture, education, public health, housing, vocational training and \neconomic revival and women’s empowerment, particularly war widoes.  Towar ds this \neffort Governement has been utilising funds. \n \n \nThe main objective of the developmental projects being implemented by India in the \nNorthern and Eastern Sri Lank s is to assist Government of Sri Lanka in its relief, \nresettlement, rehabilitation and r econstruction efforts, including to ensure welfare and \nwell-being of the Tamils affected  by protracted civil war \n \n248 crores \n \n\n3 \n \n Palestine -India’s Annual contribution to UNRWA \n \nPrimarily for provision of food and medicines to the displaces people in the refugee \ncamps under UNRWA’s various programmes \n \n-Budgetary Support \n \nPart of US$ 10 million pledge announced during the visit of Presidsent Abbas to New \nDelhi in November 2012. \n \n-Support for Building of two Schools \n \nAn MoU was signed during the visit of President Abbas to India in November 2012 to \nbuild two schools in Palestine with the support of GOI \n \nUS$ 1 million \n \n \n \n \n \nUS$ 1 million \n \n \n \nUS$180,000 \n \n Syria -Humanitaria"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |487", "t": "Indo-China Meet on Border Issue", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.487 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02.12.2015 \n \nINDO-CHINA MEET ON BORDER ISSUE \n  \n487.  SHRIMATI K. MARAGATHAM: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Ind ian and Chinese officials met recently for the \nlatest round of talks under the mechanism set up for both \ncountries to consult and coordinate on border related issues; \nand \n \n(b)  if so, the deliberations made in the said meeting? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) & (b) The latest meeting of the Working Mechanism for \nConsultation and Coordination on India -China Boundary Affairs was \nheld in Beijing on 8 October 2015. Both sides discussed variou s \nissues pertaining to the maintenance of peace and tranquillity in the \nborder areas. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |488", "t": "Housing and Slum Development", "head": "O.I.H \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION  \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 488 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 02, 2015 \n \nHOUSING AND SLUM DEVELOPMENT \n \nNo. 488 \n  \nSHRI LAXMI NARAYAN YADAV: \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is planning to implement the Integrated \nHousing and Slum Development Programme in Madhya Pradesh; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, area-wise; \n(c) the details of work done by the Government for slum development during \nthe last three years in the State; and  \n(d) the amount spent for the said work? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n(SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO) \n \n \n(a & b): Under Integrated Housing and Slum Development Programme \n(IHSDP), 50 projects with a total project cost of Rs.235.34 crore involving Rs. \n160.31 crore of central share for construction of 13635 dwelling units (DUs) \nhave been approved in  Madhya Pradesh. Details of the projects, area-wise, \nare at Annexure-I. \n \n(c) & (d): The details of work done by the Government for slum development \nin the State of Madhya Pradesh and amount spent during the last three years \nunder BSUP and IHSDP components of JNNURM as well as under Rajiv Awas \nYojana (RAY) are at Annexure-II. \n \n*****\n \n\nScheme No.\tof\t\nProjects\nProject\nCost\nCentral\t\nShare\nCentral\t\nShare\t\nReleased\nDwelling\t\nUnits\t\nSanctioned\nConstruction\t\nCompleted\nDUs\tIn‐\t\nProgress\nFunds\t\tReleased\t\t\nduring\tLast\t\nthree\tyears\tand\t\nCurrent\tYear\t\nConstruction\t\ncompleted\t\nDuring\tLast\t\nthree\tyears\tand\t\nCurrent\tYear\t\nBSUP 21 473.44    230.75    268.56      24728 21736 2992 37.02             12655\nIHSDP 50 235.34    160.31    197.31      13635 11345 2290 60.55             9802\nRAY 8 444.32     229.65    190.70      8123 -             2434 58.77             -                \nTotal 79 1,153.10 620.71    656.58      46486 33081 7716 156.35           22,457          \nDetails of work done by the Government for slum development during the last three years in the state \nof Madhya Pradesh\nAnnexure - II\n(Rs. in Cr.)\nAnnexure referred to LS USQ No: 488 due for 02.12.2