\n \n(a)\n \nw\nhether the Government has launched/proposes to launch any scheme with hundred per \ncent subsidy to provide single point electricity connection to the people living below poverty line \nin the country ;\n \n \n(b)\n \nif so, the details there\nof, State/UT\n-\nwise including Chhattisgarh; and\n \n \n(c)\n \nthe number of BPL families benefited under this scheme during the last three years and the \ncurrent year, State/UT\n-\nwise?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL & NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \n(INDEPENDENT\n \nCHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)\n \n \n(a)&(b):\n \nYes Madam.\n \n \nErstwhile RGGVY was launched by Government of India in April, 2005 for creation of \nRural Electricity Infrastructure & Household Electrification, envisaging providing access to \nelectricity to rural househol\nds and providing free electricity connections to all BPL households. \nNow erstwhile RGGVY has been subsumed in Deendayal Upadhyay Gram JyotiYojana as Rural \nElectrification component of DDUGJY. \nAs informed by REC u\nnder the scheme, 921 projects have \nbeen sanc\ntioned in the country covering release of free electricity connections to 3.96 crore BPL \nhouseholds including Chhattisgarh. Cumulatively, as on 31.10.2015, free electricity connections \nto 2.26 crore BPL households (57%) have been released.\n \n \n(c):\n \nThe State \nwise details of BPL families benefited under the scheme during the last three \nyears and current year, are presented at Annexure\n-\nI.\n \n****\n \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure I\n \nAnnexure I \nreferred to in reply \nto \nPart (c) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question \n \nN\no\n. 750 to \nbe answered on\n \nThursday, 3.12.2015\n \nState\n-\nwise  release of free electricity connections to  BPL households under DDUGJY \n(erstwhile RGGVY) during last three years and current year\n \nSr. \nNo.\n \nState\n \nDuring 2012\n-\n13                                         \nDuring 2013\n-\n14                                         \nDuri