rmulate a policy to approve big power  \nprojects within a stipulated time period; and \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the current status thereof? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR POWER,  \nCOAL AND NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY \n \n( SHRI  PIYUSH GOYAL ) \n \n(a) :  As per Section  7 of the Electricity Act, 2003, any generation company \nmay establish, operate and maintain a generating station without obtaining a \nlicense/permission if it complies with the technical standards relating to \nconnectivity with the grid.  Therefore, approval  of Government for setting up power \nprojects is not required. \n \n(b) :  In view of (a), does not arise. \n \n \n********** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |762", "t": "Calicut International Airport", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 762\n(To be answered on the 3rd December 2015)\n \nCALICUT INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the present status of the re-carpeting works of Calicut International\nAirport; and\n(b) the expenditure likely to be incurred thereon and the expected time of\ncompletion of the same?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) & (b): The work of strengthening and re-carpeting of the runway with\na timeline of 18 months has already started from 18th September 2015\nwith an expected expenditure of Rs.5611.18 lacs.\n \n*****\n762. SHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN\n be pleased to state:-\n (Dr Mahesh Sharma)"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |763", "t": "Nirmal Gram Puraskar", "head": " \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Drinking Water and Sanitation \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.763 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 3-12-2015 \nNirmal Gram Puraskar \n \n763. SHRI PONGULETI SRINIVASA REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION be pleased to state: \n(a) Whether the Government has  discontinued/proposes to discontinue the  Nirmal Gram \nPuraskar after reviewing the  efficacy of the scheme and consequent to  the launch of Swachh \nBharat Mission (SBM), if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to formulate a scheme to incentivise State  Governments \non the basis of their performance towards achieving the goals of SBM; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the  number of panchayats reported to have  achieved the status \n‘open defecation-free panchayats’ in the country, State/UT-wise; and \n \n(d) whether any target has been set  under SBM to make the rural areas open  defecation-free and \nif so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n(SHRI RAM KRIPAL YADAV) \n(a) Yes Madam. The Nirmal Gram Puraskar (NGP) has been discontinued. \n \n(b) Yes Madam. The Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin)  guidelines provide for incentivizing \nStates on the basis of their performance. \n \n(c) A World Bank Project to incentivize the Sta tes on the basis of certain performance indicators \nis under consideration. Ministry has issued the guidelines for Open Defecation Free ( ODF) \nverification. Integrated Management Information System ( IMIS) Module for ODF verification \nhas also developed. States are request to complete the process of ODF verification of all existing \nODF villages/GPs and report on IMIS  by 31 st December, 2015. However, the number of Open \nDefecation-Free Gram Panchayat s as on 30 -11-2015 as reported by the States on the IMIS of \nMinistry is at Annexure-1. \n \n(d) The Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) has a goal to achieve Swachh Bharat by 2 nd October, \n2019.  \n\n \n \n \n \nAnnexure-1 \nStatement referred in part (c) of the reply to Lok  Sabha Un-starred Question No. 763 due \nfor reply on 3-12-2015 \n \nState/UT-wise, number of Gram Panchayats  declared Open Defecation Free as on       \n30-11-2015 \n  \nState/UT ODF -GPs \nAndhra Pradesh 108 \nArunachal Pradesh 72 \nAssam 10 \nBihar 9 \nChhattisgarh 445 \nD & N Haveli 0 \nGoa 0 \nGujarat 3 \nHaryana 833 \nHimachal Pradesh 1507 \nJammu & Kashmir 10 \nJharkhand 5 \nKarnataka 197 \nKerala 0 \nMadhya Pradesh 446 \nMaharashtra 2988 \nManipur 0 \nMeghalaya 577 \nMizoram 20 \nNagaland 0 \nOdisha 13 \nPuducherry 0 \nPunjab 589 \nRajasthan 796 \nSikkim 10 \nTamil Nadu 978 \nTelangana 573 \nTripura 10 \nUttar Pradesh 126 \nUttarakhand 15 \nWest Bengal 209 \n  10549 \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |764", "t": "CAPART", "head": "O.I.H.\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 764\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015\nCAPART\n764. SHRI RAM TAHAL CHOUDHARY:\nSHRI LAXMAN GILUWA :\nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) the nature and scope of schemes approved by the Council for Advancement of People's\nAction and Rural Technology (CAPART) in Jharkhand during the last two years;\n(b) whether the work under these schemes has commenced, if so, the details thereof and if\nnot, the reasons therefor;\n(c) whether the Non-Governmental Organisations (NGOs) through which the work under\nthe said schemes is being undertaken are monitored; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\n(SHRI SUDARSHAN BHAGAT)\n(a): Council For Advancement of People’s Action and Rural Technology (CAPART)\nhas not approved any scheme in Jharkh and during the last two years as funding has been\nkept under abeyance.\n(b)to(d): Question does not arise in view of (a) above.\n*******"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |765", "t": "Psychometric Evaluation of Pilots", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 765\n(To be answered on the 3rd December 2015)\n \nPSYCHOMETRIC EVALUATION OF PILOTS \n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Ministry has created any framework to conduct\npsychometric evaluation of pilots;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) if not, the steps taken to implement a system to screen psychological\nfitness of pilots;\n(d) whether the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) has\nrecorded any cases of pilots reporting stress during the last three years\nand the current year; and\n(e) if so, the details thereof and the remedial steps taken by the\nGovernment in this regard?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (b) A working group has been formed at the Institute of Aerospace\nMedicine, Bangalore under Indian Air Force for formulating guidelines\nfor carrying out specific tests concerning psychological evaluation of civil\naircrew. The working group also has one member from DGCA.\n(c) Does not arise.\n(d) No Madam, there were no such cases reported.\n(e) Does not arise.\n \n*****\n765. SHRI OM BIRLA\n be pleased to state:-\n (Dr Mahesh Sharma)"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |766", "t": "Air Services of Private Companies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 766\n(To be answered on the 3rd December 2015)\n \nAIR SERVICES OF PRIVATE COMPANIES\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the number of private aviation companies operating aircraft services\nat present in the country;\n(b) whether the Government is implementing/proposes to implement any\nscheme for expansion of the existing airports in the country; and\n(c) if so, the details thereof?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a):  At present there are 136 private aviation companies operating\naircraft services in the country, out of which 11 are scheduled and 125 are\nnon-scheduled operators.\n(b) & (c): No, Madam. However, upgradation and modernization is an\nongoing process depending upon the traffic potential demands from\nairline operators, commercial viability etc. Hence, Ministry of Civil\nAviation and respective airport operators take initiatives to upgrades the\nairports at regular intervals.\n \n*****\n766. SHRI ARJUN MEGHWAL\n be pleased to state:-\n (Dr Mahesh Sharma)"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |767", "t": "Biomass Based Energy", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO. 767\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.1\n2\n.2015\n \n \nBIOMASS BASED ENERGY\n \n \n+767.\n \nDR. BANSHILAL MAHATO\n:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of \nNEW AND RENEWABLE EN\nERGY\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nw\nhether Bio\n-\nenergy is one of the important sources of electricity in the rural areas in \nvarious States in the country;\n \n \n(b)\n \nif so, the details thereof and the details of funds sanctioned and utilized by various states \nfor electricity generation through Bio\n-\nmass along with the outcome thereof, during each of the \nlast three years and  the current year;\n \n \n(c)\n \nwhether a large number of Bio\n-\nmass based electricity generation units are lying unused \nor functioning below their installed capacity due to low tariff; and\n \n \n(d)\n \nif so, the details thereof and reformative/corrective steps being taken by the \nGovernment in this regard?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL & NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)\n \n \n(a):\n \nYes, Madam.\n \n \n(b):\n \nThe \ngovernment does not have a scheme to finance the states directly for biomass \npower/cogeneration projects, however the Government encourages setting up of biomass \npower cogeneration projects in the country by providing financial incentives in the form of \nsu\nbsidy and fiscal incentives such as accelerated depreciation, relief from taxes and duties, \nterm loan from Indian Renewable Energy Development Agency (IRERDA) and other financial \ninstitutions including nationalized banks.\n \n \n(c):\n \nNo Madam, \nfew plants are not\n \nfinding the operations economically viable in view \n \nof \nincreased prices of biomass \ndue to other competitive users like brick kiln and cooking\n.\n \n \n(d):\n \nMinistry of New and Renewable Energy \nis pursuing \nwith SERCs\n \nto notify the tariffs as \nper guidelines of Cen\ntral Electricity Regulatory Commission (CERC) as some of the SERCs \nsuch as \nGujarat.\n \nKarnataka\n, Madhya Pradesh, Odisha and Tamil Nadu have fixed lower tariffs \nthan CERC.\n \n \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |768", "t": "Excessive Rates of Airlines", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 768\n(To be answered on the 3rd December 2015)\n \nEXCESSIVE RATES OF AIRLINES\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether some airlines have been reportedly charging\nexhorbitant/excessive rates for economy class travel on domestic routes;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the Government proposes to regulate the economy class\nairfare for domestic routes; and\n(d) if so, the details and the present status thereof along with the other\nsteps taken by the Government in this regard?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) Air fares are not controlled by the Government. Airline are free to fix\ntariff under the provision of Sub-rule (1) of Rule 135, Aircraft Rules 1937\nhaving regard to all relevant factors, including the cost of operation,\ncharacteristics of service, reasonable profit and the generally prevailing\ntariff. A Tariff Monitoring Unit has however been set up  in Directorate\nGeneral of Civil Aviation (DGCA) to monitor airfares on certain routes\nselected on random basis to ensure that the airlines do not charge airfares\noutside the range declared by them. The analysis on random basis has\nshown that the airfares remained well within the fare bucket uploaded by\nthe airlines on respective websites.\n \n(b) Does not arise.\n \n(c) No, Madam.\n \n(d) Does not arise.\n768. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR MONDAL\n be pleased to state:-\n (Dr Mahesh Sharma)\n\n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |769", "t": "Import of Textile Machinery", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.769 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015 \n \nIMPORT OF TEXTILE MACHINERY \n \n769.  DR. VIRENDRA KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government proposes  to simplify the process of import of \ntextile machinery; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the time  by which a final decision is likely to \nbe taken by the Government in this regard; and \n \n(c)  the efforts being made by the Government to augment the textile exports? \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज  ् य मंरी (स्त्वतंर प्रभार) (श्री संतोष कु मार गंगवार) \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nIN THE MINISTRY OF TEXTILES \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n(a) & (b) : The process of import of Textile machinery is already \nsimple. No proposal to further simplify the import of such \nmachinery is under consideration. \n \n(c):      Government has taken following initiatives to augment the \ntextile exports:-   \n(i)   MEIS Scheme under new Foreign Trade Policy 2015-20.  \n(ii)  Restoring Interest rate subvention for pre and post shipment \ncredit for the textile sector, \n(iii) Expanding the scope of Merchandise Export from India \nScheme (MEIS) since 29.10.2015 to 110 ne w tariff lines and \nincrease rates or country coverage or both for 2228 existing \ntariff lines.   \n(iv) Increased Duty Drawback rates for some textile articles. \n(v)  Market Access Initiative (MAI) Scheme. \n(vi) Market Development Assistance (MDA) Scheme. \n(vii) Duty Free import of trimmings, embellishments and other \nspecified item under Export Performance Certificate \nEntitlement Scheme. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |77", "t": "Scrapping of Courses by IGNOU", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SHIPPING \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.77 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 3RD DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nNON- MAJOR PORTS  \n \n*77. SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE: \nWill the Minister of SHIPPING be pleased to state: \nपोत प�रवहन मंत् \n(a) whether the minor and inter-mediatory ports plays a dominant role in \ncountry’s trade and commerce; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government proposes to set up low cost non- major ports to \nresolve the issue of the waiting period for the ships, if so, the details \nthereof; and \n(d) whether the Government has identified the coastline sites under Sagarmala \nProject for the purpose and if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF SHIPPING \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI) \n \n(a)to(d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (D ) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 77 TO BE ANSWRED ON 3 RD DECEMBER, 2015 \nRAISED BY SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE REGARDING NON- MAJOR \nPORTS \n \n(a)to(c):As per Section 3 (9) the Indian Ports Act, 1908, the respective State \nGovernments have jurisdiction over Ports other than Major Ports which are also \ncalled Non-Major Ports. There are 200 such Non-Major Ports which are under the \nState Governments. The traffic handled by Non-Major Ports is 44.74% of total \ntraffic during 2014-15. There is no proposal under consideration for setting up of \nlow cost Non-Major Ports in Ministry of Shipping. \n(d)     As a part of the Sagarmala project a national perspective plan is developed \nand identification of coastal site is also included. \n***** \n \n  \n\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |770", "t": "Creation of Authority for Renewable Energy", "head": " \n  \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO. 770\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015\n \n \n \nCREATION OF AUTHORITY FOR RENEWABLE ENERGY\n \n770\n.\n \nSHRI \nVENKATESH BABU T.G\n:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of \nNEW AND RENEWABLE EN\nERGY\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government has any proposal to create a National Authority of Renewable \nEnergy (NARE) at the Centre and similar authorities at the State level:\n \n(b)\n \nif so, the details thereof along with the proposed functions of the authority;\n \n(c)\n \nthe time by which NARE is likely to be set up;\n \n(d)\n \nwhether it is also proposed to set up a National Renewable Energy Technology Commission; \nand\n \n \n(e)\n \nif so, the details there\nof and the time by which it is likely to be set up?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL & NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)\n \n \n(a):\n \nNo, Madam.\n \n \n(b):\n \nDoes not arise.\n \n \n(c):\n \nDoes not arise.\n \n \n(d):\n \nNo, Madam.\n \n \n(e):\n \nDoes not arise.  \n \n******\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |771", "t": "Number of Vehicles Daily used National Highway", "head": "भारत सरकार  \nसड़क पररवहन और राजमार्ग मंत्रालय \nलोक सभा  \n         \nललखित प्रश् न सं.  777  \nर्ुरुवार, 3 दिसम् जर, 2075/72 अग्रहायण, 7937 (शक) \n \nराष्ट्रीय राजमार्ग पर िैननक रूप से चलने वाले वाहनों की संख्या  \n771. डॉ. रववन्द्र जाजू:  \nक्या सड़क पररवहन और राजमार्ग मंत्री यह बताने की कृपा करेंगे कक:  \n(क) क्या राष्ट्रीय राजमागग संख्या-24 की वतगमान लेन उस पर प्रततदिन चलने वाले वाहनों की \nआवश्यकता को पूरा करने के ललए उपयुक्त है;  \n(ख) राष्ट्रीय राजमागग-24 पर दिल्ली-उत्तर प्रिेश सीमा से डासना तक प्रततदिन चलने वाले \nवाहनों की वगग-वार संख्या ककतनी है;  \n(ग) क्या सरकार ने दिल्ली-उत्तर प्रिेश सीमा से डासना मागग तक राष्ट्रीय राजमागग-24 का \nववकास/चौडीकरण करना आरंभ ककया है;  \n(घ) यदि हां, तो तत्संबंधी ब्यौरा क्या है और उक्त प्रयोजनार्ग जारी/आबंदित तनधधयों का ब्यौरा \nक्या है; और  \n(ङ) इस पररयोजना को कब तक पूरा ककए जाने की संभावना है? \n \nउत् तर \nसड़क पररवहन और राजमार्ग मंत्रालय में राज् य मंत्ररी \n(श्ररी पोन्. राधाकृष्ट् णन) \n \n(क):   जी नहीं । \n(ि):   68,962 यात्री कार यूतनि (पीसीयू) प्रततदिन । \n(र्) से (ड.):  ववद्यमान यातायात घनत् व को ् यान में रखते हुए सरकार ने दिल् ली-मेरठ \nएक् सप्रेसवे (डीएमई) पररयोजना के भाग के तौर पर  सेंिर में 6 लेन के एक् सप्रेसवे सदहत   \nदिल् ली/उत् तर प्रिेश सीमा से डासना तक ववद्यमान राष्ट् रीय राजमागग सं .24 को 14 लेनों में \nचौडीकरण करने का तनणगय ललया है ।  तनवविाएं आमंत्रत्रत की गई हैं जजसमें तनवविाएं प्रस तुत \nकरने की अंततम ततधर् 15.12.2015 है और पररयोजना के शुरू होने से 30 माह में इसे पूरा \nककया जाना तनधागररत है ।  \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |772", "t": "Solar Energy Corporation of India", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO. 772\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.1\n2\n.2015\n \n \n \nSOLAR ENERGY CORPORATION OF INDIA\n \n+772.\n \nSHRI   NANA PATOLE\n:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of \nNEW AND RENEWABLE EN\nERGY\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nw\nhether the Government has approved to grant company status to Solar Energy \nCorporation of India;\n \n \n(b)\n \ni\nf so, the details thereof;\n \n(c)\n \nt\nhe reasons and objectives behind granting status of company to the REC/SEC of India; \nand\n \n(d)\n \nt\nhe\n \ndetails of the energy generation projects proposed to be setup by the said company?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL & NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)\n \n \n(a)&(b):\n \nSolar Energy Corporation of India (SECI) was incorporated in Sept. 2011 as a \ncompany under Section 8 of the Companies Act, 2013. \nGovernment has granted approval  for \nconversion of the existing Section 8 company into a Section 3 company under the Companies \nAct, \n2013 (No.18 of 2013) and for renaming it as Renewable Energy Corporation of India. \n \n \n(c):\n \nThe organization has to take up commercial activities including trading of power in order \nto implement various Govt.’s Schemes and to become self\n-\n \nsustaining. Th\ne organization is also \nrequired to \ntake up development of all segments of Renewable Energy viz. geo\n-\nthermal, off\n-\nshore \nwind, tidal, etc., apart from Solar Energy.\n \n \n(d):\n \nCurrently, the organization is engaged in implementation of a number of renewable energy \nprojects and schemes including setting up of 2000 MW solar power projects under VGF scheme, \n750 MW of solar power projects under VGF scheme, Solar Park Scheme, roof\n-\nto\np projects and \nprojects in association with other Ministries/ organizations.  \n \n******\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |775", "t": "Rebates/Concessions to Handloom Weavers", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.775 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015 \n \nREBATES/CONCESSIONS TO HANDLOOM WEAVERS \n \n775.  SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of the rebates/concessions being given to handloom weavers at present including \nthe number of handloom weavers  benefitted in various States across the  country especially in \nMaharashtra during each of the last three years and till date; \n \n(b) whether a large number of  applications have been received from cooperative  societies and \nother organisations of weavers for providing additional rebates  and concessions to handloom \nweavers; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof for the last three years and till date; and \n \n(d) the steps taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज  ् य मंरी (स्त्वतंर प्रभार) (श्री संतोष कु मार गंगवार) \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nIN THE MINISTRY OF TEXTILES \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n(a):    Marketing Incentive is given to the handloom agencies  for preparing conditions, which \nare conducive to marketing of handloom products  @ 10 % of average sales of last three years, \nwhich is equally shared by State and Central Government. The agency is expected to use this \namount towards activities that would a ttract the consumers in order to gear up overall sales of \nhandloom goods. The assistance towards Marketing Incentive (MI) is given to State handloom \ncorporations, apex co-operative societies, primary handloom weavers co -operative societies & \nnational level handloom organizations.  \n    \nDetails of releases made during the last three years to across the country including \nMaharashtra  till date with number of weavers benefitted is as follow:- \n \nSl. \nNo. \nFinancial  \nYear \nAmount \n released for   for \nMaharashtra \n(Rs.in lakh) \nTotal Released \n(Rs.in lakh) \nNo. of  \nWeavers \nbenefitted in    \nMaharashtra \nNo. of  \nWeavers \nbenefited  \nacross the  the \ncountry. \n(i) (ii) (iii) (iv) (v) (vi) \n1. 2012-13 62.41 8767.32 14,208 1746005 \n2. 2013-14   - 3461.24 - 579878 \n3. 2014-15   - 2272.69 - 148677 \n4. 2015-16 \n(Upto Nov.15) \n  - 4072.00 - 274360 \n   \n\n(b) to (d):  There is no provision for additional rebate.   \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |777", "t": "Investment by CIL", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COAL \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 777 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015 \n \nInvestment by CIL \n \n777. SHRI A. ARUNMOZHITHEVAN: \n SHRI JANAK RAM: \n  \nWill the Minister of COAL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether delay in construction of railway infrastructure in some of the major coalfields \nparticularly Bagli rail line has affected the production of coal;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Coal India Limited has produced 494 million tonnes of coal and even though this \nwas three per cent lower than the targeted 507 million tonnes, the production registered an incremental \ngrowth of record 32 million tonnes as compared to with cumulative growth of 31 million tonnes in the \nfour years period from 2010 to 2014;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(e) whether the Coal India Limited proposes to invest over Rs.62,500 crore in the next five years \nwith an aim to ramp up annual production to 908 million tonnes by 2019-20; and  \n \n(f)  if so, the details thereof and the funds allocated to States for the construction of roads and ra il \ninfrastructure in coal mining areas, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF COAL, POWER \nAND NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY  (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) & (b):  Production of coal has faced evacuation constraints due to delay in construction of \nrailway infrastructure.    However, Bagli rail line is not known to Coal India Limited. \n \n(c) & (d):  Production details and incremental growth during last five years is as under: \n \nYear Production in M.T. Growth in M.T. \n2010-11 431.32 0.06 \n2011-12 435.84 4.42 \n2012-13 452.21 16.37 \n2013-14 462.42 10.21 \n2014-15 494.24 31.82 \n \n(e) & (f): Coal India Limited (C IL) has assessed a tentative capital investment of Rs. 57,000 \ncrores for the next five years to ramp -up its coal production to 908.1 Mt. from production level of \n494.80 Mt. in 2014-15, as part of the road map for production of 1 BT coal by 2019-20. \n           \n…../-   \n\n:: 2 :: \n \n The year-wise tentative capital investment projection are as follows: \n \nCIL 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 Total \nCapital investment \n(Rs.Crores) \n5990.5 8282 14539 14635 13529 56975.5 \nsay 57000 \n  \n Further, CIL has envisaged to invest Rs. 8615.69 crores in three major Railway infrastructure \nprojects namely Tori -Shibpur in CCL ( Jharkhand), Jharsuguda-Barapalli in MCL(Orissa), East and \nEast-West corridor in SECL (Chattisgarh) for coal evacuation .                                                                                                                            \n<><><>  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |778", "t": "Conversion of State Highways into NHs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS  \n   \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 778 \nANSWERED ON 3RD DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nCONVERSION OF STATE HIGHWAYS INTO NHS \n \n778.  SHRI P. KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS, \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has decided  to convert some State Highways into  National \nHighways; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, including  the State of Tamil Nadu, where the State  Highways are \nlikely to be converted into National Highways; and \n(c) the amount of money allocated for this purpose and the likely target set for completion?  \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n(a) to (c) Declaration of National Highway (NH) is a continuous process and expansion of \nNational Highway network is taken up from time to time depending upon requirement of \nconnectivity, inter -se-priority and availability of funds.  Subsequent to declaration as NH, t he \nstretches are entrusted to an agency for development and maintenance. Development is taken \nthereafter in stretches keeping in view the inter -se priority and availability of funds. As such, no \nallocation of funds is made at the time of declaration of NH. \n \n***** \n \n  \n \n  \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |779", "t": "International Airport Norms", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 779\n(To be answered on the 3rd December 2015)\n \nINTERNATIONAL AIRPORT NORMS\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the norms prescribed for international Airports;\n(b) whether Gaya Airport is of international standards, if so, the details\nthereof;\n(c) the details of flights operating daily from Gaya airport;\n(d) whether there is a regular flight of Air India from Gaya to Delhi, if so,\nthe details thereof;\n(e) if not, the reasons therefor; and\n(f) whether the Government proposes to start regular flights from Gaya\nto Delhi and if so, the details thereof?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a): Declaration of an airport as International Airport depends upon\nvarious factors like traffic potential, demand from airlines for operation\nof international flights, availability of the facilities like suitable length of\nRunway to cater to medium capacity long-range aircraft or equivalent\ntype of aircraft, scope for extending the runway length further as per\nfuture requirements for large bodied air crafts, availability of Ground\nLighting Facilities and Instrument Landing System for operation of\naircraft at night and availability of Customs, Immigration, Health and\nAnimal & Plant Quarantine services.\n(b): Gaya is a declared customs airport. However, international flights\nare operating from Gaya.\n(c) & (d): The details of flights being operated per week by various\nairlines at Gaya Airport are as under:\n Domestic - Air India (7)\n779. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SINGH\n be pleased to state:-\n (Dr Mahesh Sharma)\n\n International - Air India (4), Myanmar Airways (4), Druk Air (3), Mihin\nLanka (1), Thai Airways (7)\n Druk Air (from December 2015 to March 2016) and Mihin Lanka\n(November 2015 & from February to March 2016) will be operating\nflights from Gaya Airport.\n Presently, Air India is operating following flights:\n - Delhi-Gaya-Varanasi-Delhi (daily)\n - Delhi-Gaya-Yangoon-Gaya-Delhi (once in a week)\n(e): Does not arise.\n(f): Flight operations in domestic sector have been deregulated and the\nairlines are free to operate anywhere in the country subject to Route\nDispersal Guidelines (RDG) issued by the Government. It is upto the\nairline  operators to provide air services to specific places depending upon\nthe traffic demand and commercial viability.\n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |78", "t": "Creation of various Tourist Circuits", "head": "������������������� �\n������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n���������������������� �������\n������������ ����� ����� �\n�\n������������������������������������ �\n�\n������������������������������