����������������� �������� ������ �������� ������������ �������� ������������ ������������������������ ������������������ ������ �������� ������������\n����������������������������������\n�� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n���������� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n������������ ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������� �������� ���������������������������������� �������� ������������ ������������������������ ������������������������ ��������������\n������������������\n��\n���������� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n�������� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������� ������������������������ ������������������ ���������� ���� �������������� ������ �������� �������������� ������������ �������� ������������\n���������������������� ���������� ������������ ���������� ���� �������������� ������ �������� ������������ ������������ ������������������ �������� ������������������\n���������������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |830", "t": "Accidents in Coal Mines", "head": "1 \n \n \n \n   GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COAL \n                                   \n LOK SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 830 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON  3.12.2015 \n \nAccidents in Coal Mines \n        \n830.   SHRI TAMRADHWAJ SAHU: \n   \n Will the MINISTER OF COAL be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the number and nature of accidents occurred in various coal mines of Chhattisgarh including the number of \npersons died during the last three years and the current years; \n(b) whether any committee /inquiry has been constituted to probe such accidents;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof;  \n(d) the action taken by the Government against the guilty found responsible for such accidents; and  \n(e) the corrective steps being taken by the Government to improve the safety of the workers in coal mines of \nChhattisgarh? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF COAL, POWER AND NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY (SHRI \nPIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a): Based on the information received from the office of Director  General of Mine Safety (DGMS),  the number and nature of \naccidents (fatal/serious) along with the number of persons died in various coal mines of Chhattisgarh during last  the three \nyears and the current year are as under : \n\n2 \n \n \nNumber of fatal and serious accidents and number of persons killed/injured  in coal mines of \nChhattisgarh during 2012-2015* \nYear \nFatal Serious \nNo. of Accidents Fatalities S/Injured No. of \nAccidents S/Injured \n2012 9 10 1 22 22 \n2013 9 9 0 19 20 \n2014 8 8 1 30 30 \n2015* 7 7 0 6 6 \n*: as on 31.10.2015 \n \n(b)to(d): In case of fatal accidents, under the provision of the Mines Act, 1952; officers of Director General of Mine Safety \n(DGMS)  conduct enquiry to ascertain the cause of accidents. These enquiries also identified the person responsible for the \naccidents. In the light of enquiries, suitable actions under relevant  provisions of Mines Act, 1952 are proposed against the  \nreasons identified to be responsible for it.  However, in case of serious accidents, generally the enquiries are conducted at the \nmanagement level. The details of fatal accidents that took place in coal mines of Chhattisgarh during last three years and the \ncurrent year along with the action taken, if any, on each case is given at Annexure.  \n \n(e): Steps taken to prevent such accidents in various coal mines, include the following:- \n \n(i) Replacement of manual loading and transportation at the coal faces by mechanized drilling, loading and \ntransportation;  \n\n3 \n \n \n(ii) Continuous environment monitoring in gassy mines for forewarning of any accumulation of inflammable ga s, \npresence of noxious gases including Co, Co2 and deficiency of oxygen in mine atmosphere;  \n \n(iii) Replacement of l ow capacity loading and transport machinery by high capacity machines in open cast mines , for \nreducing the traffic in mines and accidents in opencast operations; \n \n(iv) Initiatives for improving the skills of the operators and competent persons using most modern training aids like \nsimulators, 3D Artificial Intelligent Audio-Visuals;   \n \n(v) Promotion and propagation of safety awareness in mines. \n  \n(vi) Ensuring Worker’s participation and sensitization in matters of safety through training in safety and by initiatives \nlike celebration of safety week and safety campaigns, etc. \n \n(vii) Safety training programmes for Managers and    Supervisors for improving safety standards in mines. \n \n(viii) Introduction of Risk Assessment Techniques aimed at elimination of risks and to ensure safety of workmen. \n \n(ix) Standard operating procedures to avoid unsafe practices in mines. \n \n(x) Organising special safety awareness campaign to increase awareness of  mine workers  (i.e., ‘Safety is My \nResponsibility’). \n \n**** \n  \n\n4 \n \n \n                                                                     Details of fatal accidents in coal mines in Chhatisgarh during 2012 – 2015                                                       \nAnnexure \nYear Name of Mine Owner Date of \nAccident Killed S/Inj. Brief Cause Name of persons held \nresponsible Action taken \n2012 WEST JHAGRAKHAND SECL 13-Feb-12 1 1 Fall of Roof Suresh Kumar,Mining Sirdar Increment withheld \n              Chandrabhan,Overman Increment withheld \n              Satyendra Singh,Asst.Manager Warned by Management \n2012 \nBALRAMPUR 10&12 \nINCLINES SECL 29-Feb-12 1 0 \nOther Non-Transportation \nMachinery Misadventure No action required \n2012 MAHAN-II SECL 10-May-12 1 0 Other Electrical Accidents A.K.Dey,Manager Warned by Management \n              M.K.Chaturvedi,Safety Officer Warned by Management \n              Mangal Yadav,Helper (Deceased) No action \n              Subedar Azad Singh,C/Carrier Removed from service \n              Kuldip Singh Hoda,Work Superv. Removed from service \n              Parwan Kumar,Work Supervisor Removed from service \n2012 DIPKA MINE NO.IA SECL 14-Jun-12 1 0 Dumpers Rajendra Pd.Khatkar,Sirdar (Deceased) No action \n2012 REHAR U/G MINE SECL 16-Jul-12 1 0 Dumpers A"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |831", "t": "Pollution Control Certificates", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 831 \nANSWERED ON 3RD DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nPOLLUTION CONTROL CERTIFICATES \n \n831. SHRI RAJESH KUMAR DIWAKER: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nlM+d ifjogu vkSj jktekxZ ea=h \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of agencies/authorities authorised to issue Pollution Control Certificates to vehicles; \n \n(b) whether there is any provision to penalise vehicle owners who fail to take pollution certificates \nfor their vehicles within fixed time limit; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether there is any system to identify the number of vehicles without pollution co ntrol \ncertificate as well as the total number of vehicle owners who do not get issued the pollution control \ncertificate in time; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof along with the number of vehicles plying without certificate, State-\nwise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE       \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n(a)      As per Rule 115(7) of Central Motor Vehicles Rules, 1989, after the expiry of a period of \none year from the date on which the motor vehicle was first registered, every such vehicle shall \ncarry a valid “Pollution under control” certificate issued by an agency authorised for this purpose \nby the State Government. Central Government do not centrally maintain the details of \nagencies/authorities authori sed to issue Pollution Control Certificates to vehicles  by the State \nGovernment.     \n \n(b) & (c)  As per Section 190(2) of Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 , any person who drives or causes or \nallows to be driven in any public place a motor vehicle, which violates the standards prescribed in \nrelation to road safety, control of noise and air -pollution, shall be punishable for the first offence \nwith a fine of o ne thousand rupees and for any second or subsequent offence with a fine of two \nthousand rupees.  \n \n(d) & (e) Ministry do not centrally maintain any data of vehicles plying without pollution under \ncontrol certificate.      \n ***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |832", "t": "Private Participation in Drinking Water Schemes", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n \nLOK    SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 832 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015 \n \n \n \nPrivate Participation in Drinking Water Schemes \n \n \n832.  SHRI GANESH SINGH: \nSHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WAT ER AND SANITATION be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government to collaborate with private sector companies/ \ncorporate houses for drinking water and sanitation schemes in the country, if \nso, the details thereof, State/UT-wise including Bihar; \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to provide assistance to the States for this \npurpose; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken/likely to be taken by the \nGovernment in this regard; \n \n(d) whether certain corporate houses have come forward and submitted their \nproposals for promotion of sanitation and drinking water projects in the \ncountry; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof, corporate house-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n(SHRI RAM KRIPAL YADAV) \n \n(a) to (e) Yes Madam,  Regarding provision of drinking water to the rural \npopulation there is no proposal before the Government to collaborate with \nprivate sector companies/ corporate houses.  However, under Corporate Social \nResponsibility (CSR) many private companies have come forward to  provide \n\n \n \nsupport in the rural water supply schemes at the village / Gram panchayat level \nin the form of water purification systems in the rural schools, angan wadis and \npanchayat buildings across the country .  Under Swachh Bharat Mission \n(Gramin), Guidelines have been issued to facilitate the utilization of Corporate \nSocial Responsibility (CSR) funds in rural sanitation activities. States can use \nthese guidelines as a base to develop their own procedure to attract/receive and \nutilize CSR funds. Swachh Bharat Kosh has been set up under the Ministry of \nFinance to attract contributions from Corporat es and other entities towards \nachievement of Swachh Bharat. The contribution to Swachh Bharat Kosh by \nthe companies has also been covered under CSR under the Companies Act.  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |833", "t": "Incentives to Farmers Using Solar Energy", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO. 833\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.1\n2\n.2015\n \n \nINCENTIVES TO FARMERS USING SOLAR ENERGY\n \n \n \n+833.\n \nSHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA:\n \nSHRI DADDAN MISHRA:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of \nNEW AND \nRENEWABLE ENERGY\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government is providing subsidy/incentives under any of its schemes to the \nfarmers in rural areas for promoting Solar Energy, if so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(b)\n \nwhether the Government has any proposal to\n \nenhance incentives being given to the farmers;  \n \n \n(c)\n \nif so, the details thereof; and \n \n \n(d)\n \nif not, the reasons therefor?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR POWER, COAL & NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL)\n \n \n(a):\n \nMinistry is providing subsidy upto 30% for general category and 90% for special category \nStates including for farmers under “Off\n-\nGrid & Decentralized Solar Applications” scheme which \ncovers solar lightings, solar water pumps, solar lanterns, mini/micro gri\nd etc. with focus in rural \nareas for promoting Solar Energy. Irrigation using solar pump is major initiative of the government \nand so far 94,870 nos. of solar irrigation pumps have been sanctioned, which are being allotted to \nfarmers by the State Governmen\nts.\n \n(b),(c)&(d):\n \nThe current scheme provides good incentives for the farmers for promotion of solar \nenergy. \n \n*******\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|6|UNSTARRED |834", "t": "Dilapidated Condition of NHs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 834 \nANSWERED ON 3RD DECEMBER, 2015 \n \nDILAPIDATED CONDITION OF NHS \n \n \n834. SHRI FEROZE VARUN GANDHI:  \nSHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY:  \nSHRI SUKHBIR SINGH JAUNAPURIA: \n  SHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER:  \nSHRI RAYAPATI SAMBASIVA RAO: \n  SHRI C.S. PUTTA RAJU:  \nSHRI KANWAR SINGH TANWAR: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसडक परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of the dilapidated condition of National Highways across the country during \nthe last three years and the current year, State/UT-wise;  \n(b) the amount of funds allocated and spent for the same during the last three years, \nState/UT-wise; and \n (c) the steps taken by the Government for repair and renovation of NHs across the country? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n(a) to (c)  Development and Maintenance of National  Highways is continuous process. The \nmain reasons of the dilapidated condition of certain stretch of NHs are due to availability of \ninadequate resources  for maintenance of NHs and inadequate pavement  \nthickness/composition of state roads while handing over to the central government after its \ndeclaration as national highway.  However, National Highways are developed and kept in \ntraffic worthy condition within the available resources and depending on inert-se-priority. In \nstretches under implementation , the maintenance is carried out by the \ncontractor/concessionaire as part of t heir obligations in the contract.  The fund allocated and \nexpenditure thereon for development & maintenance of National Highways during the last \nthree years and the current year are Annexed.   \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART S (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 834 ANSWERED ON 03.12.2015 ASKED BY  SHRI \nFEROZE VARUN GANDHI,  SHRI RAVINDRA KUMAR PANDEY,  SHRI SUKHBIR \nSINGH JAUNAPURIA, SHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER,  SHRI RAYAPATI SAMBASIVA \nRAO, SHRI C.S. PUTTA RAJU  AND SHRI KANWAR SINGH TANWAR   REGARDING \nDILAPIDATED CONDITION OF NHS \n \n \nFunds allocated for development & maintenance of National Highways during last three \nyears and current year \nRs. in Crore \n \n \n \n \nSl. \nNo State/UT \nAllocation for developement of National \nHighways \nExpenditure for developem